    "definition": "High-block passing options and forward passes on matches 1925299 and 1996435. The screening defender is the outfield opponent closest to the segment from the ball carrier to the teammate, with segment parameter t in [0.10, 0.90]. Body between ball and teammate: that defender is within 1.5 m of the segment. Facing the lane: a reliable shoulder heading is within 45 degrees of the direction from that defender to the ball, so the chest looks back along the lane toward the passer. Shoulders are reliable when both are present, width is between 0.15 and 0.60 m, and the worse p90 error is at most 15 cm. Heading is the left-to-right shoulder axis rotated +90 degrees. Shadow-screen requires both the lane occupation and the facing. If the lane is occupied but the shoulders are missing or unreliable, the event is excluded. If nobody is in the lane window, the event is not a shadow-screen. Tracking picks the defender. Pose supplies only the heading. Forward means pass_ahead. Completion is pass_outcome successful versus any other recorded outcome. Pass value is pass_epv_total. Influential is the option xthreat, compared inside the same possession, and separately a within-match split of players above versus below the median number of passes played or received. Goalkeepers are excluded. Segments shorter than 1 m are excluded. No xG.",
